[h2]0.8.0[/h2]
[h3]Progression sets[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Clear material ladders[/b], like vanilla wood and metal: Deep Ore → Deep Iron → Steel → Alloy, Crude Oil → Chemical → Polymer, stone → brick → cement → concrete, and gears → machine cores → electronics → power modules.
[*][b]Renamed:[/b] Deep Alloy is now Deep Iron, and High-Grade Steel is now Steel. Saves keep their stock.
[*]Steel is made from deep iron, coal and limestone (was metal blocks). Chemical is made from crude oil and extract (was badwater); chemical from brine is unchanged.
[*][b]Building costs climb the ladders:[/b] early buildings cost logs, planks, gears and bricks; industrial ones add concrete, metal blocks and deep iron; then steel and treated planks; frontier buildings use alloy and machine cores; endgame buildings add electronics and power modules. Costs are worth about the same as before and still match what each building looks like.
[*][b]Fixed a deadlock:[/b] the Deep Drill wears metal block drill bits instead of steel, which it could never get before the Steel Mill. The Deep Mine and Deep Well still use steel bits.
[/list]

[h3]Roofs are platforms[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]No more roof railings, parapets or curbs.[/b] Flat roofs, terraces and balconies are open platforms: paths join across neighbouring roofs at the same height, and buildings can be built across the edge where two roofs meet. The Restaurant's chairs and tables are lower, so diners no longer hit the ceiling.
[/list]

[h3]Bricks: a new step between metal and concrete[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]New good: Brick.[/b] The Stone Crusher grinds sandstone into dirt (brick earth), and the Cement Kiln fires dirt and water into bricks, burning logs.
[*][b]The Cement Kiln unlocks at 600 science[/b] (was 900), together with the crusher, so bricks come before concrete (1,000). The kiln is also cheaper to build.
[*]Cement is made from limestone and dirt again, and concrete from sandstone, cement and water, with the same amounts as before.
[*]Buildings with brick walls and plinths now cost bricks: 19 buildings, from the Concrete Mixer to the Rocket Assembly Hangar. The crusher and kiln never need bricks.
[*]The kiln now accepts Timber Pipes for its brick water.
[*]The vanilla Terrain Block unlocks at 2,000 science with the Dirt Excavator (was 1,000).
[/list]

[h3]Brick art[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Brick looks like brick:[/b] a painted red brick texture with pale mortar replaces the modelled orange courses on every brick building below, and the brick buildings are much lighter on triangles.
[*][b]Brick Block:[/b] the Limestone Masonry Block is now a red brick block (4 bricks and 1 cement). Placed limestone blocks turn into brick blocks.
[*]Brick plinths on the Deep Drill and Deep Ore Processor; the Coal Power Plant's bright concrete base is now dark brick.
[*]Brick ground floors on the Public Health Lab, Technical School and Food Packaging Works, and on the Water Treatment Plant's chemical house.
[*]The Concrete Mixer's footings and the quarries' plinth walls are brick; the quarries now cost bricks.
[*]Brick footings under the Restaurant's and Fishery Works' deck posts.
[*]Limestone outcrops and seams look like grey rock now, not white gems.
[/list]

[h3]Seven goods removed[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Aggregate:[/b] concrete uses sandstone, cement uses dirt.
[*][b]Flux:[/b] steel uses limestone instead.
[*][b]Compost:[/b] the Fertilizer Works makes fertilizer in one step; the Greenhouse needs fertilizer to build.
[*][b]Medical Food, Emergency Ration, Packaged Food:[/b] the Food Packaging Works makes canned fish. The flight course uses canned fish, and the Grocery Store stocks eggplant rations.
[*][b]Archive Data:[/b] Mission Control reads recovered artifacts directly. Human Record Caches give artifacts, and story chapters 5 and 6 count artifacts.
[*][b]Old saves keep working:[/b] stored goods turn into their replacement (Aggregate into sandstone, Flux into limestone, Compost into fertilizer, the three foods into canned fish, Archive Data into recovered artifacts).
[/list]
